course: dictionary
lesson: 7338
title: Plaque: one word, three meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, so use the context to find the right one. «A sticky film called plaque, full of bacteria, grows on your teeth every day» tells you plaque is on teeth, so it means the germ film, not a sign.
explain: «Families sometimes pay for a bench, tree or plaque in a place the person loved» gives different clues: a bench, a tree, a place the person loved. Here a plaque is a flat sign that remembers someone.
explain: Check your meaning with the swap test. Put "sign" into the teeth sentence: "a sticky film called sign grows on your teeth" makes no sense, so the sign meaning is wrong there. Read the clues first, then test your meaning in the sentence.
fact: Plaque is a soft, sticky film of germs (bacteria) that forms on your teeth.
fact: «Plaque» causes tooth decay and gum disease if it is not brushed away.
fact: A plaque can also be a flat piece of metal, stone or wood with writing on it, fixed to a wall to remember a person or event.
fact: Blue plaques on houses show where famous people lived.
fact: In medicine, plaque can mean a fatty build-up inside blood vessels.
exercise: «A sticky film called plaque grows on your teeth every day.» What is plaque here? | *A sticky film of germs on your teeth | A kind of bench in a park | A tooth that has fallen out | A flat sign on a wall
exercise: «Families pay for a plaque in a place the person loved.» What is a plaque here? | *A flat sign with writing, fixed to a wall | A fatty build-up inside blood vessels | A sticky film of germs
exercise: «Sugar feeds the bacteria in plaque.» What do the bacteria do with the sugar? | Ignore it | Wash it away | *Feed on it and make acid | Turn it into a sign
test: «Plaque» is a noun with more than one meaning. Which meaning fits «a plaque on the wall» with writing on it? | A fatty build-up in the blood | A sticky film of germs | *A flat sign fixed to a wall | A kind of toothpaste
test: Why do dentists tell you to brush away plaque? | Because plaque makes your teeth grow longer | Because plaque is a famous person | *Because it causes holes in your teeth and gum disease | Because plaque tastes of sugar
exam: Jayden says plaque always means a sign on a wall. Which clue in «It comes from bacteria living in a soft sticky film on your teeth, called plaque» proves him wrong? | The word called | The word bacteria is a hard word | *The words soft sticky film on your teeth | It comes from
